.. dropdown:: Technical details
    :class-container: dk-default-value

    The filename of the font to use. The path may be absolute or relative.
    Relative paths are resolved using :func:`~kivy.resources.resource_find`.

    .. warning::
        Depending on the active text provider, the specified font file may be
        ignored. In most cases, however, it works without issues.

        If the selected font does not contain the glyphs required for the
        language or symbols you are displaying, missing characters will appear
        as blank box placeholders ('[]'). To avoid this, choose a font that
        includes the necessary glyphs.

    .. note::
        When the default value is `None`, Kivy falls back to the ``Roboto`` font.
        This default is taken from :class:`~kivy.config.Config`.

